    <string name="editor_help_title">ABC notation help</string>
    <string name="editor_help">Header lines (before the music):\nM:6/8 meter · L:1/8 default note length · Q:1/4=100 tempo · K:D key (G, Ador, Em, Amix…)\n\nNotes: C D E F G A B (low octave), c d e f g a b (high octave), c\' one octave higher, C, one octave lower. z is a rest.\n\nLengths: A2 double, A3 dotted, A/2 or A/ half. A&gt;B dotted rhythm, (3ABc triplet, A-A tie.\n\nAccidentals: ^F sharp, _B flat, =F natural.\n\nBars and repeats: | bar, |: … :| repeat, [1 … :|[2 … alternate endings, |] end.\n\nThe whistle key is chosen automatically. You can paste any tune in ABC format (from thesession.org for example).</string>
